    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nMiniAI\n\n### Description\n\nI know this has been mentioned before:\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/116\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/123\r\n\r\nAnd i'm aware from the docs that this is by design, but if given the following buffer:\r\n```\r\n{\r\n...stuff...\r\ncurrent -> | <- line {brackets}\r\n...stuff...\r\n}\r\n```\r\nThen `vi{` will select `next` rather than `cover`. For me I'm happy with that behaviour *most* of the time, but there are times where I really want the covering brackets, and it can be a pain to get them if there's a \"next\" in the way. \r\n\r\nIn the same way we can currently \"force next\" in a scenario like: `(cursor | stuff (parens))`, we can select the `parens` by using `vin(` to force `next` rather than `cover`, my proposal is to add the ability to force `cover`. Maybe `vic{` which would basically act like a temporary switching of the config from `cover_or_next` to be `cover`.\r\n\r\nWhy not just use `cover` in my config? Well most of the time I really like the `cover_or_next` behaviour and it's what I want, so changing the config isn't really ideal.\r\n\r\nI was able to get it working in a few lines of code(though the credit goes to the quality of the existing code, I didn't really do much)\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.ai/compare/main...pejrich:mini.ai:main\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if this is something you even want added. I've left the mapping blank by default so it's opt in, but it's not something that appears possible to implement purely from my own config, since it requires some internal functions, otherwise I'd just happily do it there.\r\n",
