            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n> Why not just use `cover` in my config? Well most of the time I really like the `cover_or_next` behaviour and it's what I want, so changing the config isn't really ideal.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, this is the suggested way to resolve this issue. I'd even say more: if the \"last\"/\"next\" mapping variants were part of the initial 'mini.ai' release, there would not have been a configurable `search_method` in favor of an explicit usage of preferred mapping (default \"cover\", \"last\", or \"next\").\r\n\r\nAs this need occurs not that often, another approach is to use consecutive application in Visual mode. In the example above, the `va}a}` can select the covering braces.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
